Use max_chunk_bytes as the canonical upload chunk (t268 stage 1)

The shell file contract (Sophia d040013bb) defines the upload chunk as
max_chunk_bytes directly. ContentResourceBegin::layout no longer derives
it from the socket frame, min(max_frame_payload - 48, max_chunk_bytes).

The two expressions are equal on every valid Limits object, because
ContentLimits::validate still requires max_chunk_bytes + 48 <=
max_frame_payload, and max_input_queue_bytes >= max_frame_payload + 24.
Both relations, the scalar bounds and the encoded Limits bytes are
unchanged. The IPC crate is untouched.

tests/upload_chunk_layout.rs pins the rule. It checks one fixed chunk
under frame caps at the +48 boundary, one past it and at the cap, with
exact-row and single-row chunks. It checks the canonical chunk counts
through the file upload record, the mandatory +24/+48 relations at their
boundaries, and the golden Limits bytes. It passes with either expression
by design.
